# Error Ownership And Recovery

- If generated code fails to build, run, or parse, treat it as an agent failure and fix it immediately
- Do not ask the user to diagnose or explain errors caused by generated code
- Do not provide self-justifying explanations or postmortems unless the user explicitly asks for one
- Keep user-facing error responses brief and action-oriented: acknowledge, fix, verify, report
- After a failure report, prioritize correction over discussion
- Before reporting completion, verify the touched logic by reading the changed files and using editor lints
- Do not run compile or test commands to verify; propose them if a Maven check is still needed
- If verification is blocked, state exactly what was verified and what remains
